+++ b/docs/windows-guest-pages-16k.md
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+# Fixed 16 KiB guest-page experiment on Windows x64
+
+The opt-in `guest-page-16k` feature selects 16 KiB for all guest ABI page constants in the library. Without it, x64 builds retain their 4 KiB behavior. Host virtual-memory mapping remains at the actual host page size. A feature-enabled DLL cannot serve mixed 4 KiB and 16 KiB guests.
+
+The upstream per-device design is YahiaAngelo/reims-vgpu commit `84089ca48a08b258c2c784ccf01976be020a0c08`, present in vphone pin `960bf4b128a2678f032e46eb32964caa4828b818`. Its changes to about 50 files do not apply cleanly to this Windows baseline, particularly Windows section backing and C API layout. This smaller compile-time option is an experimental capability, not that complete port. Existing source licenses apply.
+
+Build in a Visual Studio developer shell with Rust 1.98.1, one Cargo/CMake job and debug/incremental output disabled:
+
+```
+cargo build -p reims-vgpu-c --no-default-features --features vulkan,guest-page-16k
+cargo test -p reims-vgpu-core --features guest-page-16k guest_page_constants_
+clang tests/windows-guest-pages-16k.c -Icrates/reims-vgpu-c/include target/debug/reims_vgpu_c.dll.lib -o guest-pages-16k.exe
+```
+
+Put `target/debug` on the process PATH. Run the executable without arguments, then with `boundary`, `unaligned-length` and `outside`. The normal and final-page cases require exact 8192-byte GPU readback; invalid length and out-of-map start require zero guest frames/callbacks. The fixture is based on the upstream EFI sequence in `tests/suite/scenarios/smoke_host.py`.
+
+Observed on 2026-11-03, NVIDIA RTX 4070 Ti / native Windows:
+
+- Feature build passed (4m41s), retaining existing LNK4098 MSVCRTD conflict warning.
+- Page-geometry unit test passed (one test; full suite not run).
+- Both positive fixtures matched every output byte; invalid 12 KiB length and outside start were rejected with zero presents.
+- A separate Dynarmic A64 fixture executed 2048 framebuffer stores and seven 16 KiB-page MMIO writes, then obtained exact GPU output through this DLL.
+
+These tests prove a bounded GPU presentation path. They do not qualify full FIFO, IOSurface, suspend/resume, guest Metal compatibility or iOS boot, nor settle the mixed CRT warning for production use. No existing VM was modified by the tests.
